<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term · script</p><h1 class="enc-title">Asomtavruli</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mrgvlovani</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Asomtavruli is the oldest form of the Georgian alphabet, written with rounded letters. Its earliest dated inscriptions, from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolnisi-sioni">Bolnisi Sioni</a> church and the Georgian monastery at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bir-el-qutt">Bir el Qutt</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bethlehem">Bethlehem</a>, belong to the fifth century. It was later supplemented by the Nuskhuri and Mkhedruli scripts and is still used for capitals and headings in church texts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/asomtavruli.jpg" alt="Asomtavruli" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Emperor of Emperors · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kartuli,_Georgian_scripts.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
